statement:
Let $Y$ be a scheme [def-pc-scheme] with small etale site $Y_{\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-etale-site]. For a $Y$-scheme $P$ let $h_P$ be the presheaf of sets on $Y_{\Et}$ with $h_P(U)=\operatorname{Mor}_Y(U,P)$, restriction along $U'\to U$ being composition. Call a sheaf of sets $\mathcal F$ on $Y_{\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaf-of-sets] *finite locally constant* if there are a covering $\{Y_i\to Y\}_{i\in I}$ of $Y_{\Et}$ and finite sets $S_i$ such that for every $i$ the restriction $\mathcal F|_{Y_i}$ (the sheaf $U\mapsto\mathcal F(U)$ on $(Y_i)_{\Et}$, an etale $Y_i$-scheme being an etale $Y$-scheme through $Y_i\to Y$) is isomorphic to the constant sheaf $\underline{S_i}$ on $(Y_i)_{\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-constant-sheaf]. Then:

1. for every finite etale morphism $P\to Y$ [def-weil-pbc-finite-etale-category] the presheaf $h_P$ is a sheaf of sets on $Y_{\Et}$ and is finite locally constant;
2. every finite locally constant sheaf of sets $\mathcal F$ on $Y_{\Et}$ is isomorphic to $h_P$ for some finite etale morphism $P\to Y$.
